{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UGQmXbsYT7QWWj2bRfaLph","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519/projects/nlp_variance_gtheory/literature_map.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"meta:\\\\n  last_updated: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20T14:00:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n  total_papers: 10\\\\n\\\\ncategories:\\\\n  - key: \\\\\\\"gtheory_evaluation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    name: \\\\\\\"G-Theory & Evaluation Variance\\\\\\\"\\\\n    narrative: \\\\\\\"Applying Generalizability Theory and variance decomposition to LLM evaluation reliability\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - key: \\\\\\\"infrastructure_variance\\\\\\\"\\\\n    name: \\\\\\\"Infrastructure-Induced Variance\\\\\\\"\\\\n    narrative: \\\\\\\"Hardware, precision, and CUDA-level nondeterminism as variance sources in LLM inference\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - key: \\\\\\\"prompt_sensitivity\\\\\\\"\\\\n    name: \\\\\\\"Prompt Sensitivity & Methodological Variance\\\\\\\"\\\\n    narrative: \\\\\\\"Prompt phrasing, seed, temperature, and ordering as variance sources\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - key: \\\\\\\"evaluation_methodology\\\\\\\"\\\\n    name: \\\\\\\"Evaluation Methodology\\\\\\\"\\\\n    narrative: \\\\\\\"Scoring artifacts, benchmark design, and evaluation protocol considerations\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\npapers:\\\\n  mesting2026hidden:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Hidden Measurement Error in LLM Pipelines Distorts Annotation, Evaluation, and Benchmarking\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Mesting, F.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.11581\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"gtheory_evaluation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"direct-competitor\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Closest methodological precedent: G-theory decomposition of 5 facets (item, prompt, temperature, judge model, replication) on AILuminate/MMLU/Chatbot Arena. Found judge model=43.8%, prompt×judge=12.4%. Critically excludes infrastructure factors — our work extends this by crossing infrastructure with methodology.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20T14:00:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  brittlebench2026:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Brittlebench: Quantifying LLM Robustness via Prompt Sensitivity\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: []\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.13285\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"prompt_sensitivity\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"direct-competitor\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Up to 50% performance variance from prompt perturbations, 63% of cases show ranking reversals from single perturbations. Provides perturbation protocol we follow for prompt paraphrase generation. Does not cross with infrastructure factors.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20T14:00:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  yuan2025layercast:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Understanding and Mitigating Numerical Sources of Nondeterminism in LLM Inference\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Yuan, Z.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.09501\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"infrastructure_variance\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"direct-competitor\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Documents up to 9% accuracy variation and 9,000-token response-length shifts from GPU count, type, and precision changes. Proposes LayerCast (FP16 storage + FP32 compute) mitigation. Does not conduct factorial attribution across multiple variance sources.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20T14:00:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  messina2026background:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Introducing Background Temperature to Characterise Hidden Randomness in LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Messina, P.\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Scotta, A.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.22411\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"infrastructure_variance\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"method-component\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Formalizes hidden nondeterminism as effective background temperature T_bg persisting even at nominal T=0 due to floating-point non-associativity in BF16/FP16. Provides theoretical framework for understanding infrastructure-level stochasticity we measure.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20T14:00:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  generalizit2024:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"GeneralizIT: A Python Solution for Generalizability Theory Computations\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: []\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.17880\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"gtheory_evaluation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"method-component\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Python implementation of G-theory computations including D-study projections. Core analysis tool for our variance decomposition pipeline.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20T14:00:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  hua2025flaw:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Flaw or Artifact? Rethinking Prompt Sensitivity in Evaluating LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Hua, W.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"EMNLP\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"evaluation_methodology\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"evaluation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Demonstrates log-likelihood-based evaluation inflates apparent prompt sensitivity — a confounder our generation-based evaluation protocol controls for. Motivates our choice of generation-based scoring.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20T14:00:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  thinkingmachines2025batch:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Batch Invariance, Seed Locking, and Beyond: Countering Nondeterminism in LLM Inference\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: []\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Technical Report\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"infrastructure_variance\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"method-component\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Shows 80/1000 unique completions for Qwen3-8B at T=0 under default vLLM settings. Demonstrates batch-invariant GEMM/RMSNorm/attention kernels eliminate nondeterminism with 1.6-2.1x latency overhead. We use DEFAULT settings (without these kernels) to reflect practitioner conditions.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20T14:00:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  kunievsky2025intent:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Measuring Intent Comprehension in LLMs: A Variance Decomposition Framework\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Kunievsky, D.\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Evans, J.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.16584\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"gtheory_evaluation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"direct-competitor\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Decomposes variance into intent, articulation, and model uncertainty facets. Does not include infrastructure factors. Provides alternative facet structure we compare against.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20T14:00:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  bui2025seeds:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Assessing the Macro and Micro Effects of Random Seeds on Fine-Tuning Large Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Bui, T.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"prompt_sensitivity\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"background\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Documents extreme seed sensitivity (RTES variance=18.22) in fine-tuning. Motivates our fine-tuning G-study extension. Isolated factor study without infrastructure crossing.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20T14:00:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  sameprompt2026:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Same Prompt, Different Outcomes: Evaluating the Reproducibility of Data Analysis by LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: []\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.14349\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"prompt_sensitivity\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"background\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Evaluated 2 strategies x 6 models x 4 temperatures with 10 repeats but excluded hardware/precision. Confirms methodology-layer variance without infrastructure crossing.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20T14:00:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 6732, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RdahfyKVtwMwAfTJrn7pUJ","session_id":"e13969ce-5d2d-4a82-903b-b87fae4e296f","uuid":"d50f7a1f-b5a7-48cc-9ccf-c48931762b24","timestamp":"2026-05-20T23:32:16.775Z"}
