{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RdahfyKVtwMwAfTJrn7pUJ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review submitted. Here is the summary:\n\n**Score: 4/6 (Weak Accept), High Confidence**\n\nThe review covers the median-tier dream paper for `dream_20260520T222113`. Key findings:\n\n**Improvements over Dream #1 (all acknowledged):**\n- Model-as-facet analysis now properly separates model×item interaction (16-22%)\n- Bootstrap CIs added on key variance components\n- Five benchmarks with three-tier narrative\n- Infrastructure separability reframed as confirmatory\n- Bibliography expanded from 9 to 18 references\n\n**New methodological concerns raised (not in Dream #1):**\n1. **Binary data in G-theory** — standard Henderson III / REML assume continuous responses; binary 0/1 data violates these assumptions, and item_id dominance is partially artifactual from the Bernoulli variance function\n2. **Temperature (2-3 levels) and ordering (4 systematic rotations) as random facets** — too few levels and non-random selection violates exchangeability assumptions\n3. **Asymmetric designs across benchmarks** — MMLU includes FP32 but other benchmarks do not, confounding the cross-benchmark precision gradient\n4. **Separability overstated in abstract** — holds on 3/5 benchmarks but fails on GSM8K (3.0%) and MATH (2.5%)\n\n**10 questions for authors** covering negative variance estimates, fixed vs. random temperature, cross-benchmark precision comparisons, D-study optimization procedure, double bootstrap, answer extraction methods, and more.\n\n**Verdict:** At the acceptance threshold contingent on addressable revisions (binary data discussion, temperature sensitivity analysis, MMLU BF16/FP16-only cross-benchmark comparison, abstract qualification of separability). Report saved to `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519/projects/nlp_variance_gtheory/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T222113/median/review_report.md`."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a1382c0317ef91356 (use SendMessage with to: 'a1382c0317ef91356' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 99190\ntool_uses: 26\nduration_ms: 265237</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e13969ce-5d2d-4a82-903b-b87fae4e296f","uuid":"3cde38b7-d717-407f-a7fd-9843269f92d8","timestamp":"2026-05-20T23:36:25.560Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1) for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept). Your focus areas are **methodology** and **experimental rigor**.\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"Reproducibility Budgets for LLM Evaluation: A Generalizability Theory Analysis of Variance Sources Across Benchmarks, Models, and Evaluation Metrics\"\n\nThe paper applies Generalizability Theory (G-theory) to LLM evaluation, conducting a multi-benchmark crossed-facet variance decomposition. Three facet classes: measurement (item_id, 200 stratified items per benchmark), methodology (prompt template ×6, random seed ×6, temperature ×2-3, option ordering ×4), infrastructure (numerical precision FP32/BF16/FP16/LayerCast, GPU hardware ×2 types). Six models (4×7-9B + 2×14B), five benchmarks (MMLU, ARC-Challenge, HellaSwag, GSM8K, MATH), over 4 million evaluation records.\n\nThree claims:\n1. **Cross-benchmark variance gradient**: item_id dominance is benchmark-conditional — 56% on MMLU down to 21% on MATH, a 35pp monotonic gradient driven by CoT stochasticity shifting variance into temp×item and seed×item interactions.\n2. **Confirmatory separability null**: direct infra×methodology interactions are negligible (<0.3%), validating isolated-factor studies at the aggregate level, though both factor types interact substantially with items.\n3. **D-study protocol reversal**: optimal evaluation protocol reverses across task types — MMLU is item-limited (420 items for G≥0.90), GSM8K is seed-limited (10 seeds for G≥0.90). Current practice G<0.25 everywhere.\n\n## Key Methods Details\n- Variance estimated via Henderson's Method III (expected mean squares), with REML as sensitivity check (difference <1.4pp, identical rankings).\n- All inference uses vLLM V0 engine in enforce_eager mode, eliminating an engine confound discovered in pilot (default vLLM routes FP32 through V1 CUDA graph vs V0 eager for BF16/FP16, inflating precision effects by ~6pp).\n- Model treated as crossed random facet in comprehensive analysis (Section 7), reducing item_id by ~7pp and residual from 20.7% to 12.0%.\n- Bootstrap CIs via 1,000 item-level resamples; all CIs exclude zero, no adjacent benchmark pair overlaps.\n- D-study projections use the G-theory formula G = σ²_o / (σ²_o + Σ σ²_fj/n_fj + Σ σ²_fjfl/(n_fj·n_fl) + ...).\n- Item resampling stability test: 3 independent stratified 200-item MMLU samples, CV=4.1% for item_id.\n\n## Experiments in the paper:\n1. **MMLU full-scale G-study** (Section 4): 4 models × 3 precisions × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 3 temps × 4 orderings × 200 items = 1,036,800 records. Table 1 (variance decomposition), Table 2 (per-model), Table 3 (resampling stability).\n2. **Cross-benchmark gradient** (Section 5): ARC, HellaSwag, GSM8K each 460,800 records; MATH 460,800 records. Tables 4-7.\n3. **Multi-hardware separability** (Section 6): 2 GPU types × full MMLU design = 691,200 records. Tables 8-9.\n4. **Comprehensive analysis** (Section 7): model-as-facet reanalysis, bootstrap CIs, D-study projections. Tables 10-15.\n5. **14B scale extension** (Section 8.1): Qwen3-14B, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-14B, 345,600 records. Table 16.\n6. **Fine-tuning G-study** (Section 8.2): RoBERTa-large on SST-2/MNLI/RTE/COPA, 1,728 runs. Tables 17-18.\n7. **LayerCast precision** (Section 8.3): 172,800 records. Table 19.\n8. **Appendices**: MATH per-model (Table 20), logprob scoring (Appendix B), higher-order interactions (Appendix C).\n\n## Experiments in the design document NOT fully in paper:\nThe design document (review_context.yaml) lists 8 imagined experiments (exp-001 through exp-008). The paper covers all 8 experiments but some details are condensed:\n- exp-001 (MMLU full-scale): fully covered in Section 4\n- exp-001b (item resampling): covered in Section 4.3\n- exp-002 (cross-benchmark): covered in Section 5\n- exp-003 (multi-hardware): covered in Section 6\n- exp-004 (comprehensive analysis): covered in Section 7\n- exp-005 (14B extension): covered in Section 8.1\n- exp-006 (fine-tuning): covered in Section 8.2\n- exp-007 (LayerCast): covered in Section 8.3\n- exp-008 (MATH): covered in Section 5.2\n\nSo the paper appears to have good coverage of the planned experiments.\n\n## Your Review Task\nProduce a detailed review focusing on:\n1. **Methodological soundness**: Is the G-theory framework correctly applied? Are the variance estimation methods appropriate? Are the crossed random-effects assumptions justified?\n2. **Experimental design**: Are the factorial designs adequate? Are there missing controls or confounds? Is the item sampling strategy sound?\n3. **Statistical rigor**: Are the bootstrap CIs properly constructed? Are the D-study projections valid? Is the REML sensitivity check sufficient?\n4. **Reproducibility concerns**: Are there aspects of the experimental setup that could threaten reproducibility of the findings themselves?\n5. **Strengths and weaknesses** (bulleted lists)\n6. **Questions for authors** (numbered)\n7. **Minor issues**\n8. **Score** (1-6) with confidence (low/medium/high)\n\nBe thorough and critical but fair. Report in structured markdown.","agentId":"a1382c0317ef91356","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review submitted. Here is the summary:\n\n**Score: 4/6 (Weak Accept), High Confidence**\n\nThe review covers the median-tier dream paper for `dream_20260520T222113`. Key findings:\n\n**Improvements over Dream #1 (all acknowledged):**\n- Model-as-facet analysis now properly separates model×item interaction (16-22%)\n- Bootstrap CIs added on key variance components\n- Five benchmarks with three-tier narrative\n- Infrastructure separability reframed as confirmatory\n- Bibliography expanded from 9 to 18 references\n\n**New methodological concerns raised (not in Dream #1):**\n1. **Binary data in G-theory** — standard Henderson III / REML assume continuous responses; binary 0/1 data violates these assumptions, and item_id dominance is partially artifactual from the Bernoulli variance function\n2. **Temperature (2-3 levels) and ordering (4 systematic rotations) as random facets** — too few levels and non-random selection violates exchangeability assumptions\n3. **Asymmetric designs across benchmarks** — MMLU includes FP32 but other benchmarks do not, confounding the cross-benchmark precision gradient\n4. **Separability overstated in abstract** — holds on 3/5 benchmarks but fails on GSM8K (3.0%) and MATH (2.5%)\n\n**10 questions for authors** covering negative variance estimates, fixed vs. random temperature, cross-benchmark precision comparisons, D-study optimization procedure, double bootstrap, answer extraction methods, and more.\n\n**Verdict:** At the acceptance threshold contingent on addressable revisions (binary data discussion, temperature sensitivity analysis, MMLU BF16/FP16-only cross-benchmark comparison, abstract qualification of separability). Report saved to `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519/projects/nlp_variance_gtheory/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T222113/median/review_report.md`."}],"totalDurationMs":265237,"totalTokens":99190,"totalToolUseCount":26,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7797,"cache_read_input_tokens":90924,"output_tokens":468,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7797},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":468,"cache_read_input_tokens":90924,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7797,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7797,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":10,"searchCount":4,"bashCount":0,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":12}}}
